      "side": 1,
      "message": "What happens if TEE is v2 but SB is v1?\n\nI think the check above should be dropped, and instead just check `AidlVersion(tee) \u003c 2` here.\n\nIn fact, I think all of these precondition checks could be made simpler (which I should have done in my previous modification here), to just look for and check the devices used in each test.  Something like:\n\n```\nTEST_F(SecureElementProvisioningTest, TeeOnly) {\n    auto tee \u003d keymints_.find(SecurityLevel::TRUSTED_ENVIRONMENT)-\u003esecond;\n    if (tee \u003d\u003d nullptr) {\n        GTEST_SKIP() \u003c\u003c \"Test not applicable to device with no TEE KeyMint devices\";\n    }\n    if (AidlVersion(tee) \u003c 2) {\n        GTEST_SKIP() \u003c\u003c \"Test not applicable to TEE KeyMint device before v2\";\n    }\n    ...\n```\n\nWDYT?",
      "revId": "775c9d90fcde0b6340174429afcec14855f46143",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
